A||N||6||wla21841||Clock in radio always on||||5||
Z||000000||wla21841||10-05-2000||09:17 PM||||It's been five years sinse I've really been in my 84 Fiero SE. I don't remember if the light in the radio is soposed to be on when the ignition switch is off. I have a battery drain problem. It gooes down in about 4 days. I am just now putting it back on the road.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||10-05-2000||09:19 PM||||With my 88 when the car is off the radio is off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||10-05-2000||10:12 PM||||I have that problem with my 80 Cutlass.  I know it's not the same, but the older cars with the "new" digital clock stayed on all the time, with the ignition on or off.  It's also got a drain problem as well.  I just took the fuse out until I drive it.  That way, it can get recharged when I drive it every day.  It's kind of a nuisance.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||10-05-2000||11:38 PM||||The digital clock is <B>not</B> supposed to display all the time.  Only when the key is on, or if you press the knob in.<P>"It's not supposed to display all the time?  What, you  mean it's supposed to show just the minutes, or what?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sorry about that...<BR>  <BR>In case it makes you feel better, one of my Fieros developed the "clock display always on" syndrome, too.  I switched radios with another car - and the problem migrated with the radio unit.  So in my case, at least, it seemed to be in the radio unit itself.      ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Tigger||10-06-2000||12:44 AM||||I agree with Stu, the automatic 10 second turn off timer inside the radio might have died.  New factory radio might solve that.<P>The problem I have with mine is it's always loosing or gaining an hour every day or couple days.  Maybe, I'm just going forward or back in time when I'm traveling at speeds above 88 mph?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k  No serious, I think I'll probably need a new radio to fix that problem too.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||10-06-2000||08:11 AM||||I should have included this with my first post on this subject, but:<P>wla21841, FWIW, my temporary fix for the "display always on" problem was to leave the keep-alive disconnected.  The keep-alive is the 2-terminal connector in back of radio, on RHS.  Do that, and the radio still plays, but it forgets presets and won't (accurately) give you the time of day.  But you won't have to keep recharging your battery, at least!<P>Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ! ||||reg||3
Z||000006||wla21841||10-06-2000||09:40 PM||||Wall I guess that makes the decission for me. I've been wanting to puy in a CD anyway.Nows the time.<P>Thanks a lot guys.<BR>Bill||||reg||14
